---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base title="Chauncy - Private Knowledge Discovery for Your Documents" description="Chauncy helps writers, researchers, and analysts search, connect, and curate their own document collections locally. No account, no telemetry, no autonomous agents.">

  <section class="hero">
    <div class="container hero-grid">
      <div class="hero-copy">
        <p class="eyebrow">Local-first document intelligence</p>
        <h1>Your documents know more than you think.</h1>
        <p class="hero-sub">
          Chauncy helps you search, connect, and curate the material you already have: PDFs, email, notes, web clips, and long-forgotten files.
        </p>
        <p class="hero-body">
          Ask in plain English. Inspect the source. Follow the connections. Chauncy discovers what is related, but you decide what matters.
        </p>
        <div class="hero-actions">
          <a href="/pricing" class="btn btn-primary">Buy Chauncy for Windows</a>
          <a href="#safety" class="btn btn-secondary">See the privacy model</a>
        </div>
        <div class="hero-trust">
          <span>No account</span>
          <span>No cloud sync</span>
          <span>No telemetry</span>
          <span>No autonomous actions</span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="product-mockup" aria-label="Chauncy interface preview">
        <div class="mock-nav">
          <span class="mock-tab active">Workspace</span>
          <span class="mock-tab">Add</span>
          <span class="mock-tab">Settings</span>
          <span class="mock-status">Engine ready</span>
        </div>
        <div class="mock-query">What did I save about the Henderson contract?</div>
        <div class="mock-body">
          <div class="mock-results">
            <div class="mock-card selected">
              <div>
                <strong>Contract notes - February review</strong>
                <p>Mentions the renewal clause, vendor concession, and the email thread from March.</p>
              </div>
              <span>83%</span>
            </div>
            <div class="mock-card">
              <div>
                <strong>Email from Dana about vendor terms</strong>
                <p>Connects pricing change to the amended service window.</p>
              </div>
              <span>78%</span>
            </div>
            <div class="mock-card">
              <div>
                <strong>Annotated PDF: Services Agreement</strong>
                <p>Your note: "This is the clause to challenge if renewal timing changes."</p>
              </div>
              <span>74%</span>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="mock-panel">
            <p class="mock-panel-label">Connected material</p>
            <h3>Chauncy surfaces evidence. You curate the argument.</h3>
            <p>Open a source, compare related material, add your own annotation, and keep the trail attached to the document collection.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="safety" class="section-alt">
    <div class="container safety-grid">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Private by architecture. Safe by restraint.</p>
        <h2>Chauncy is not a runaway agent.</h2>
        <p>
          It does not browse the web for you, operate accounts, send email, buy things, delete files, or chain together background actions. Chauncy is a retrieval and curation tool for your own material.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="safety-cards">
        <div class="safety-card">
          <h3>Local first</h3>
          <p>Your documents, search index, embeddings, and annotations live on your machine.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="safety-card">
          <h3>Explicit AI</h3>
          <p>AI synthesis is optional. You choose the provider, supply the key, and decide when excerpts leave your machine.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="safety-card">
          <h3>Human judgment</h3>
          <p>Chauncy can surface connections. It does not decide what is true, important, or ready to publish.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="how-it-works" class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-intro">
        <p class="eyebrow">Workflow</p>
        <h2>From scattered archive to usable evidence.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="workflow-grid">
        <div class="workflow-step">
          <span>01</span>
          <h3>Collect</h3>
          <p>Bring in PDFs, email, Markdown, Word, PowerPoint, HTML, web URLs, notes, and voice notes.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="workflow-step">
          <span>02</span>
          <h3>Ask</h3>
          <p>Use plain English to search by meaning, not just filename, folder, or exact keyword.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="workflow-step">
          <span>03</span>
          <h3>Inspect</h3>
          <p>Open the source, check the surrounding context, and see related material beside it.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="workflow-step">
          <span>04</span>
          <h3>Curate</h3>
          <p>Add your own annotations, keep the useful trail, and turn discovered material into your work.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="features" class="section-alt">
    <div class="container feature-split">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Built for serious personal archives</p>
        <h2>For people who remember the point, not the filename.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="feature-list">
        <div>
          <h3>Semantic retrieval</h3>
          <p>Find the memo, quote, email, or note even when you cannot remember the exact words.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3>Automatic connections</h3>
          <p>See related material across formats and projects without maintaining a hand-built graph.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3>Annotations that matter</h3>
          <p>Attach your intellectual response to source material: disagreement, confirmation, questions, and next steps.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3>Your AI boundary</h3>
          <p>Use local search without an API key, or opt into cloud/local AI synthesis only when you choose.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container cta-block">
      <p class="eyebrow">Windows installer is ready</p>
      <h2>Windows launch pricing is available now.</h2>
      <p>Buy once through Stripe, then download the Windows installer from the Chauncy delivery page.</p>
      <a href="/pricing" class="btn btn-primary">Buy Chauncy for Windows</a>
    </div>
  </section>

</Base>

<style>
  .hero {
    padding: 6rem 0 5rem;
  }

  .hero-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 0.92fr) minmax(520px, 1.08fr);
    align-items: center;
    gap: 3rem;
  }

  .hero-copy h1 {
    margin-top: 0.85rem;
    max-width: 740px;
  }

  .hero-sub {
    margin-top: 1.2rem;
    color: var(--color-text);
    font-size: 1.28rem;
    line-height: 1.65;
  }

  .hero-body {
    margin-top: 0.85rem;
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    font-size: 1.03rem;
    line-height: 1.75;
  }

  .hero-actions {
    margin-top: 2rem;
    display: flex;
    gap: 1rem;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
  }

  .hero-trust {
    margin-top: 1.35rem;
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0.55rem;
  }

  .hero-trust span {
    padding: 0.35rem 0.6rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    border-radius: 999px;
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.03);
    font-size: 0.78rem;
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  .product-mockup {
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border-bright);
    border-radius: 14px;
    background: #050505;
    box-shadow: var(--shadow-md);
    overflow: hidden;
  }

  .mock-nav {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 1rem;
    padding: 0.9rem 1.15rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    background: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.76);
  }

  .mock-tab {
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    font-weight: 700;
  }

  .mock-tab.active {
    color: var(--color-primary);
  }

  .mock-status {
    margin-left: auto;
    color: var(--color-success);
    font-size: 0.72rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .mock-query {
    margin: 1.4rem auto 1.15rem;
    width: calc(100% - 3rem);
    padding: 0.9rem 1rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border-bright);
    border-radius: 14px;
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    background: var(--color-bg-secondary);
  }

  .mock-body {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1.35fr 0.9fr;
    gap: 1rem;
    padding: 0 1.2rem 1.2rem;
  }

  .mock-results {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.7rem;
  }

  .mock-card,
  .mock-panel {
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    border-radius: 10px;
    background: var(--color-bg-secondary);
  }

  .mock-card {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 1rem;
    padding: 0.85rem;
  }

  .mock-card.selected {
    border-color: rgba(14, 165, 233, 0.48);
    background: rgba(14, 165, 233, 0.08);
  }

  .mock-card strong {
    display: block;
    font-size: 0.88rem;
  }

  .mock-card p,
  .mock-panel p {
    margin-top: 0.35rem;
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    font-size: 0.78rem;
    line-height: 1.5;
  }

  .mock-card span {
    color: var(--color-primary);
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    font-weight: 700;
  }

  .mock-panel {
    padding: 1rem;
    align-self: stretch;
  }

  .mock-panel-label {
    color: var(--color-primary) !important;
    font-weight: 700;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .safety-grid,
  .feature-split {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 0.85fr 1.15fr;
    gap: 3rem;
    align-items: start;
  }

  .safety-grid p,
  .cta-block p {
    margin-top: 1rem;
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    font-size: 1.05rem;
    line-height: 1.75;
  }

  .safety-cards,
  .feature-list,
  .workflow-grid {
    display: grid;
    gap: 1rem;
  }

  .safety-cards {
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
  }

  .safety-card,
  .workflow-step,
  .feature-list > div {
    padding: 1.25rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    border-radius: 8px;
    background: var(--color-surface);
  }

  .safety-card p,
  .workflow-step p,
  .feature-list p {
    margin-top: 0.55rem;
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    line-height: 1.65;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
  }

  .section-intro {
    max-width: 680px;
    margin-bottom: 2rem;
  }

  .workflow-grid {
    grid-template-columns: repeat(4, 1fr);
  }

  .workflow-step span {
    color: var(--color-primary);
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    font-weight: 750;
  }

  .workflow-step h3 {
    margin-top: 0.75rem;
  }

  .feature-list {
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
  }

  .cta-block {
    max-width: 720px;
    text-align: center;
  }

  .cta-block .btn {
    margin-top: 1.5rem;
  }

  @media (max-width: 1000px) {
    .hero-grid,
    .safety-grid,
    .feature-split {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }

    .product-mockup {
      max-width: 760px;
    }

    .workflow-grid,
    .safety-cards {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
    }
  }

  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .hero {
      padding-top: 4rem;
    }

    .mock-body,
    .workflow-grid,
    .safety-cards,
    .feature-list {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }

    .product-mockup {
      display: none;
    }
  }
</style>
